# The step of axpy_2_entry: axpy_step_2 on a scalar a and arrays x and y that the program supplies,
# every limb guarded first: those of y before they are added (rule R3), those of a and x because
# mul_2_2 takes them as factors of fused operations whose addends are not zero, where a compiler that
# sees the other factor to be 1 rewrites fma(x, 1, s) as x + s and may fuse a product of the program
# into it (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation: architecture.md; measured in the products of one
# limb, never in this one). Its claims are those of axpy_step_2: the guard is the identity on numbers
# of the format.
# Its bound, relative to the terms |a x| + |y|, from those of mul_2_2 and add_2_2, with
# eps+ = 3u^2/(1-4u): |z - (a x + y)| <= (eps+ (1 + 4u^2) + 4u^2) |a x| + eps+ |y| + (1 + eps+) 3/2 eta,
# the bound of dot_step_2, and (1 + eps+) 3/2 <= 2 from precision 4.
kernel:        axpy_entry_step_2
input:         supplied a = a0 a1
input:         supplied x = x0 x1
input:         supplied y = y0 y1
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         a*x+y
requires:      normalized a
requires:      normalized x
requires:      normalized y
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z T c=3*(1+4*u*u)/(1-4*u)+4 k=2 t=2
min_precision: 4
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v axpy_entry_step_2_correct
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v axpy_entry_step_2_ieee_bridge
ieee_spec_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v axpy_entry_step_2_ieee_correct
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v axpy_entry_step_2_ieee_lead
source:        axpy_step_2 on the guarded limbs of a, x and y (rule R3, the factors of a fused operation); bounds from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge spec

ga0      = guard(a0)
ga1      = guard(a1)
gx0      = guard(x0)
gx1      = guard(x1)
gy0      = guard(y0)
gy1      = guard(y1)
(z0, z1) = axpy_step_2(ga0, ga1, gx0, gx1, gy0, gy1)
